    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.jump\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nWhen start jumping (e.g. `fe` to jump to the next `e`) and repeat the jump with `;` an error is shown instead jumping to the next occurance. Do the next jump with `f` is working. Going backward with \"\"F\" or \",\" is also working.\r\n\r\nmini.nvim is isntalled in version 0.11.0.\r\nIt is activated in LazyVim with \r\n> require(\"mini.jump\").setup()\r\n\r\nso the defaults of https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.jump/blob/main/lua/mini/jump.lua#L95 are used\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.4\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Open a buffer\r\n2. start jumping (e.g. `fe` to jump to the next `e`)\r\n3. when pressing `;` a error is shown \r\n    > Can not jump because there is no recent `target`.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nAfter pressing `;` the cursor jumps to the next occurance of the searched character.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nAn error is shown\r\n> Can not jump because there is no recent `target`.",
