            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, I can not reproduce. The following steps worked on Neovim 0.9.5 and Neovim Nightly, on 'mini.nvim' 0.11.0 and `main`:\r\n- Open Neovim with some file containing letter `e`.\r\n- Press `f`, `e`. It jumps to the `e`.\r\n- Press `;`. It jumps again.\r\n\r\nBesides that, I am fairly confident that should work as there is a [passing test specifically for that](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0bc73241cd9c686d80ab28f4af2c04e626fb2304/tests/test_jump.lua#L811-L813).\r\n\r\nI would like to ask you for the following steps:\r\n- Execute `:map ;` to see if there is any conflicting mapping for `;`. Ideally this should show three mappings in different modes, all related to 'mini.jump'. Something like this:\r\n![screenshot_2024-02-23_12:37:31](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/24854248/a6fe1755-0db8-4b86-93f5-be6a9aec0cc7)\r\n- Disable all plugins except 'mini.jump' and try to reproduce the issue with this minimal setup.",
